> 1) I have a wand of polymorph, how should I use it? 

obviously to use a wand, you (z)ap it... I gather you know that already, so:

> I heard about polypiling
> and read the spoiler but I'm still confused on how many I should put before
> a golem is generated. Also I only have items from all the dwarf or gnome
> corpses. Will that hurt my chance of getting things like Dragon Scale Mail
> from polypiling (assuming it's even possible)?

I might say that with only huge loads of normal armor (e.g. iron skull caps,
dwarvish cloaks, iron boots) you won't be getting a lot of good items.
I'd consider it a waste to use your /polymorph on this stuff.
Did you try all those (non-cursed) armor items? Even though you already may
have boots or a helmet, you should try on more of them until you've got
some with reasonable high enchantment (say +3), although you could still
try for more. Now if you've got several enchanted items you don't need
(e.g. you have +4 boots, but also some spare +2 and +3 ones), you might 
polymorph those in hope of getting even better AC.

You can't get DSM via polypiling, and if you polymorph non-magic stuff, your
chances of receiving something magical (there are some cloaks, boots, or
helmets you would like to have) are pretty slim.

