> 5) How do I get more USEFUL items, such as wands, potions of scrolls? Nymphs
> drop object detection, which is sort of worthless and paper golems drop
> scrolls but they seem to be pretty rare and the scrolls are unlablled. Wands
> seem to be generally rare, is there a chance of a monster dropping a wand of
> wishing?

Generally the best way to get more stuff is to kill monsters, but you already
know this, as your chest full of armor shows. The best way to get useful
stuff is exploring more levels where you'll find rings, wands, amulets, and
food lying around. You may even get /wishing this way, but you shouldn't count
on that. AFAIK, there are different probabilities for object generation in
different dungeon types, e.g. in the Mines you're more likely to find tools
such as bags or lamps, and gems.
 
> 6) Finally, how do I counter against level teleport and trapdoors traps?
> They tend to seperate me from my pet, and I depend on him to live, since my
> offensive power as a healer isn't that great.

(s)earching might let you discover traps without activating them.
Also a good idea is to always go down the downstairs, as soon as you find 
them, so you know how to get back up quickly if you do fall down.

